  "worked_solution": "To compute ${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x),$ we must compute the left and right-sided limits separately.\n\nHowever, the left-sided limit ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x)$ does not exist since $f(x)$ is not defined on the interval $x\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nConsequently, the overall limit does not exist either:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$",
